  "concept": {
    "movement": "A low, predatory aerial Wyvern. Paired membrane wings drive deliberate hovering and forward flight, with a restrained torso and two tucked grasping hind talons. The long spear-tipped tail stays horizontally centered and follows the surrounding serial sections rather than flicking independently.",
    "attack": "A gathering wing stroke braces a forward neck-and-body snap. The complete horned head reaches toward the target and the hind talons advance below it, then recover coherently. This is an airborne bite/talon threat, not a transferred four-legged foreclaw rake. Independent jaw movement requires demonstrated jaw/teeth ownership first.",
    "death": "Forward loss of lift, then a controlled drop onto actual lower chest and pelvic belly. Wings slacken outside the neck, legs and tail; both hind chains release before talons relax. The serial tail lowers toward the floor while the whole body holds a stable supported ending."
  },
